@page "/derived"
@inject CharacterSession Session

<PageTitle>Derived stats — Prowlers &amp; Paragons</PageTitle>

<h1>Derived stats</h1>
<p class="muted">
    Nothing on this page is bought. All three follow from what is already on the sheet, and
    they change as you change it.
</p>

@* **No panel around these.** Each of the four figures is already a ruled box, so a bordered
   panel holding them was a box drawn around four boxes, carrying no heading and separating
   nothing from anything. The panel is what a *section* looks like; these are the section. *@
<DerivedStatBlocks WithFormulas="true" />

@* The rule for each figure is printed under the figure itself. What is left here is the
   *working* — this character's own ranks, and the three details that are easy to get wrong
   — which is the half a one-line rule cannot carry. Before this the two said the same thing
   twice on the same screen, the panel's copy being the longer and better one. *@
<Panel Title="How these came out">
    <h3>Edge</h3>
    <p class="small">
        Three details are easy to get wrong: <b>Danger Sense replaces</b> Perception rather
        than adding to it, <b>Lightning Reflexes is a flat +6</b> with no rank, and
        <b>Super Speed</b> floors Edge at its rank × 3.
    </p>

    @* The working, with the numbers actually used. This list showed Perception even when
       Danger Sense had replaced it, so the figures on the page added up to something other
       than the Edge printed above them, and there was no way to see why. *@
    <ul class="small muted">
        @if (DangerSenseRank is { } danger)
        {
            <li>Danger Sense @(danger)d stands in for Perception @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("perception")d.</li>
        }
        else
        {
            <li>Perception @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("perception")d.</li>
        }
        <li>The better of Agility @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("agility")d and Intellect @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("intellect")d.</li>
        @if (Session.Sheet.HasPower("lightning_reflexes"))
        {
            <li>Lightning Reflexes adds a flat +@DerivedStatsCalculator.LightningReflexesEdgeBonus.</li>
        }
        @if (Session.Sheet.HasPower("super_speed"))
        {
            <li>Super Speed sets a floor of its rank × 3.</li>
        }
    </ul>

    <h3>Health</h3>
    <p class="small">
        Halves always round up — the rulebook has a global rule for it in the Glossary.
    </p>
    <p class="small muted">
        Toughness @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("toughness")d,
        Might @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("might")d,
        Willpower @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("willpower")d
    </p>

    <h3>Resolve</h3>
    <p class="small">
        Determination costs @DerivedStatsCalculator.DeterminationHpPerResolve Hero Points a
        point. A specialist with a rank at the Trait Cap starts on nothing; a generalist
        starts with room to spend.
    </p>
    <ul class="small muted">
        <li>Trait Cap @(Session.TraitCap)d.</li>
        <li>@Plural(ResolveFlaws, "Condition or Plot Hook flaw", "Condition or Plot Hook flaws").</li>
        @if (DeterminationResolve > 0)
        {
            <li>Determination, bought for @DeterminationResolve more.</li>
        }
    </ul>
</Panel>

<StepButtons Back="gear" BackLabel="Gear" Next="finishing" NextLabel="Finishing touches" />

@code {
    private int ResolveFlaws => Session.Sheet.Flaws.Count(IsResolveFlaw);

    private bool IsResolveFlaw(SelectedFlaw sf) =>
        Session.Rules.GetFlaw(sf.FlawId)?.FlawType is "condition" or "plot_hook" or "plot_hook_and_condition";

    /// <summary>Danger Sense's effective rank when it is on the sheet, else null.</summary>
    private int? DangerSenseRank =>
        Session.Sheet.SelectedPowers.FirstOrDefault(sp => sp.PowerId == "danger_sense") is { } ds
            ? Session.Derived.GetEffectiveRank(ds, Session.Sheet)
            : null;

    private int DeterminationResolve =>
        Session.Sheet.SelectedPowers.FirstOrDefault(sp => sp.PowerId == "determination")?.Units ?? 0;

    /// <summary>"1 flaw", "2 flaws". Never "flaw(s)", which is a form field, not a sentence.</summary>
    private static string Plural(int count, string one, string many) =>
        $"{count} {(count == 1 ? one : many)}";
}
